<title>GERMANY: Tietmeyer won't comment on EMU status of countries.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer won't comment on EMU status of countries.</headline>
<dateline>ASCHAU, Germany 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Thursday he would not comment on the suitablity of individual countries to join European monetary union, set to begin in January 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;The Bundesbank will not comment on the situation of individual countries,&quot; Tietmeyer said at a news conference when asked how the Bundesbank would respond if the French budget deficit were to be above 3.5 percent of Gross Domestic Product.</p>
<p>But Tietmeyer said, &quot;We naturally follow the developments in individual countries as we do developments in our own.&quot;</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
